    "gaps": [
      "Helper-internal commentary-marker, assumption, bridge, derivation and finalization scans preserve native order and accumulating findings/evidence. They have no item cap, truncation, repair iteration, convergence test or exhaustion signal; no bounded graph loop is invented.",
      "Imported artifacts and callbacks execute Python. Their filesystem, network and external effects require service qualification; descriptor capability labels are not grants or a Python sandbox. The existing service read-only policy rejects import and inspection.",
      "Module handles belong to one live MCP process, carry the original imported instance and text, require matching state, and are consumed once even on inspection failure. Abandoned handles are reclaimed at server shutdown. They do not support portable artifacts or persistent resume; schemas do not fully validate Python callback results.",
      "Lunar supplies required receipts, artifact digests and execution provenance. Optional CLI output/logging, hub preflight/dry-run and write auditing remain native boundary responsibilities outside the selected reviewer graph.",
      "The retained 3600-second ceiling and four-call budget are descriptor limits enforced by Lunar. The registered hub subprocess timeout is 300 seconds; the selected native function has no timeout. No native collection-exhaustion signal is added."
    ]
  },
